{
  "method": "Unique-R^2 decomposition swept across education ceilings 20-90 in steps of 10, entry threshold fixed at 10%. For each ceiling, run three within-country FE regressions per outcome (GDP alone, Edu alone, Both) on the Maddison-backfilled GDP sample, report R^2 decomposition and joint-regression GDP coefficient/SE/p. Tests whether GDP's unique contribution concentrates at low ceilings (high-mortality / low-education countries \u2014 the Lutz & Kebede 1990-2010 child-mortality exception) and vanishes at high ceilings. Outcome-specific lags: TFR at T+LAG_TFR=5 (biological parent-of-newborn timing); U5MR at T+LAG_CHILDREARING=12 (childrearing window); LE and child education at T+LAG_GENERATION=28 (time-to-agency / edu\u2192edu).",
